1: /**
2:  * JG-035 shaft machining kinematics (leaf spec: shaft-kinematics-camera-spec, 2026-10-05).
3:  *
4:  * Closed-form machining kinematics for the 43 s Input Shaft story, sampled from one master
5:  * playhead. Everything is a pure function of time: no accumulators, no clocks, no randomness,
6:  * no allocation in per-frame paths, deterministic under any seek order.
7:  *
8:  * Frame: shaft-local millimetres, +Y is the shaft axis (CAD datum). The runtime loader performs
9:  * exactly one conversion (shaft-local +Y -> glTF -Z); nothing here converts.
10:  *
11:  * Certified tool numbers (clearance-v4 report, mirrored in toolSpec.ts):
12:  *   shaper N=20 disc cutter, signed work/cutter ratio -2, centre distance 15.5 mm,
13:  *   tip radius 11.2032 mm (near edge at root + 5 um), thickness 1.2 mm,
14:  *   stroke centre limits y 2.17..9.7749, overtravel 0.5 mm past the last tooth material,
15:  *   return backed off 2.0 mm. Hob R 5.87 mm tilted 5.5587 deg, centre distance 10.1618 mm,
16:  *   stop yc 9.5249, path: radial infeed at yc -4.195 -> feed +Y -> retract 2.5 mm -> withdraw.
17:  *
18:  * Sign conventions (tool-conventions.md, independently checked there to 1e-12 m/s):
19:  *   Shaper: tool and work axes +Y, cutter centre on +Z. Positive angles right-hand about +Y.
20:  *   External rolling at the pitch point (work z=+5, cutter z=-10 in the 5/10 mm pitch circles)
21:  *   gives phi_w = -2 * phi_c (toolSpec SHAPER_SIGNED_RATIO).
22:  *   Hob: RH one-start, axis a = [cos g, sin g, 0], shaft contact at shaft +Z = tool -Z side,
23:  *   so phi_w = -(starts / teeth) * phi_h = -phi_h / 10.
24:  */
